vations", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Dana Lee's flight and hotel are both booked and confirmed. They went through as two separate bookings instead of one combined trip.\n\n- **Flight (R0001):** F100, nonstop from SFO to JFK on 2026-11-12, **$289**. This was the cheapest nonstop. F120 costs $199 but has a stop.\n- **Hotel (R0002):** Midtown Lodge (H1), check-in 2026-11-12 for 2 nights at $189/night, **$378**. This was the cheapest New York hotel under $250/night.\n- **Total charged to the corporate card: $667.** That's under the $1000 limit, so manager approval wasn't needed.\n\n**Why there are two bookings:** The combined booking request timed out. When I retried it, the system said the first attempt had failed partway because of an error reserving the hotel. Dana's reservation list showed the flight had been booked but the hotel hadn't, so I booked the hotel on its own. A final check shows exactly one confirmed flight and one confirmed hotel, so nothing was booked or charged twice.", "type": "text"}]}]}